From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akram-composio <akram@composio.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:26:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] web: say Kimono Photos instead of Immich in English strings

Why: i18n/en.json is shared by the web and phone apps; English is the only
language Kimono reworded, and no English string may name Immich, its website,
GitHub or Discord.

What must survive upstream changes:
- No value in i18n/en.json contains "Immich" (case-insensitive). Keys are left
  alone (code references them). Product name -> "Kimono Photos"; help/admin
  wording -> "your Kimono administrator" / "whoever runs your Kimono".
- Upstream promo copy (purchase panel, "Buy Immich", version announcement,
  third-party support notice, Discord/GitHub error help) is neutral and short.
- ICU placeholders and <tags> in each value are preserved, except where the
  linked text was dropped on purpose (admin.backup_onboarding_footer).
- Only en.json is edited; other locales fall back or stay upstream.
- checks/web.sh fails on any en.json value matching /immich/i, so new upstream
  strings must be reworded when the patch is re-created.

